VALUES ('UabU9PAncho','Words of resistance – Deutsche Welle and the Greek dictatorship | DW Documentary','During Greece’s military dictatorship, Deutsche Welle was the main source of uncensored news for Greeks; an overwhelming majority tuned in every night. The Greek-language service was set up by a few brave exiled men and women. It was a beacon of press freedom, fighting fascism with words. This documentary is a personal recollection of this chapter in German-Greek history and marks the 50th anniversary of the military coup. After being forced into exile by the right-wing "Regime of the Colonels" (1967-1974), a small handful of Greek men and women set up the famous Greek-language news service broadcast every evening by Deutsche Welle. During the seven-year dictatorship an overwhelming majority of people in Greece listened to the hour-long show, which would become a beacon of press freedom and resistance. This documentary tells the story of the individuals who created the program, and who fought a prolonged struggle to give people in Greece hope and dignity. It takes an unprecedented in-depth look behind the historic role played by the Greek exiles and West Germany’s international broadcasting service during and after the junta. _______ Exciting, powerful and informative – DW Documentary is always close to current affairs and international events. Our eclectic mix of award-winning films and reports take you straight to the heart of the story. Dive into different cultures, journey across distant lands, and discover the inner workings of modern-day life. Subscribe and explore the world around you – every day, one DW Documentary at a time. Subscribe to DW Documentary: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCW39zufHfsuGgpLviKh297Q?sub_confirmation=1# For more information visit: https://www.dw.com/documentaries Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/dw.stories','https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UabU9PAncho/maxresdefault.jpg','Documentaries','DW Documentary','DW Documentary','UCW39zufHfsuGgpLviKh297Q','DOCUMENTARY','2017-04-21T17:11:43Z','','','{"id":"UabU9PAncho","title":"Words of resistance – Deutsche Welle and the Greek dictatorship | DW Documentary","description":"During Greece’s military dictatorship, Deutsche Welle was the main source of uncensored news for Greeks; an overwhelming majority tuned in every night. The Greek-language service was set up by a few brave exiled men and women. It was a beacon of press freedom, fighting fascism with words. This documentary is a personal recollection of this chapter in German-Greek history and marks the 50th anniversary of the military coup. After being forced into exile by the right-wing \"Regime of the Colonels\" (1967-1974), a small handful of Greek men and women set up the famous Greek-language news service broadcast every evening by Deutsche Welle. During the seven-year dictatorship an overwhelming majority of people in Greece listened to the hour-long show, which would become a beacon of press freedom and resistance. This documentary tells the story of the individuals who created the program, and who fought a prolonged struggle to give people in Greece hope and dignity. It takes an unprecedented in-depth look behind the historic role played by the Greek exiles and West Germany’s international broadcasting service during and after the junta. _______ Exciting, powerful and informative – DW Documentary is always close to current affairs and international events. Our eclectic mix of award-winning films and reports take you straight to the heart of the story. Dive into different cultures, journey across distant lands, and discover the inner workings of modern-day life. Subscribe and explore the world around you – every day, one DW Documentary at a time. Subscribe to DW Documentary: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCW39zufHfsuGgpLviKh297Q?sub_confirmation=1# For more information visit: https://www.dw.com/documentaries Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/dw.stories","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UabU9PAncho/maxresdefault.jpg","category":"Documentaries","city":"","country":"","channel":"DW Documentary","channelTitle":"DW Documentary","channelId":"UCW39zufHfsuGgpLviKh297Q","badge":"DOCUMENTARY","publishedAt":"2017-04-21T17:11:43Z","viewCount":29687,"durationSeconds":2546,"admission":{"version":3,"status":"channel-candidate","source":"channel-archive","mode":"DOCUMENTARIES"}}',1);
